From 71fa2f577d4781ff770807bbb48856fbb772c9c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Charliechen114514 <725610365@qq.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 22:09:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drivers/rknpu: port vendor RKNPU 0.9.x driver to mainline
 7.3.1
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Brings the vendor Rockchip NPU driver (reference/rk3588/kernel, 5.10.198
tree, build #2) onto mainline so /dev/rknpu (the legacy ioctl ABI that
librknnrt 1.5.0 and the rknn byte-exact replay engine speak) exists on
the TFTP+NFS boot path. Needed for the rknn real-board verification
line (.claude/rknn, notes/rknn 001-008).

API drift 5.10 -> 7.3.1:
- rknpu_devfreq.c replaced by a stub: the rockchip_opp_select /
  system_monitor / ipa framework does not come along; NPU runs at the
  assigned 200 MHz (byte-exact work is frequency-independent). DVFS can
  be rebuilt later on dev_pm_opp.
- drm_driver: .gem_prime_mmap and .date members removed upstream.
- vm_insert_mixed/pfn_t removed: fault handler now vmf_insert_page.
- vmap() dropped VM_MAP; iommu_map/iommu_map_sg grew a gfp_t arg.
- sg dma-bus-address marking API (sg_is_dma_bus_address etc.) removed:
  the vendored dma-iommu copy keeps the plain path. iommu_dma_cookie
  still starts with iovad, so the domain->iova_cookie cast holds.
- hrtimer_init -> hrtimer_setup; .remove returns void;
  MODULE_IMPORT_NS takes a string; rockchip_nvmem_cell_read_u8
  re-implemented on of_nvmem_cell_get/nvmem_cell_read.
- rockchip_iommu_is_enabled() poll replaced by the driver's own FPGA
  fallback (msleep 20) at the one runtime-suspend call site.
- -Werror dropped from ccflags-y (gcc 15 new warnings).

DTS: rknpu@fdab0000 node ported from vendor &rknpu (three reg windows,
one node) + &rknn_mmu_0 enabled; mainline rknn-core nodes (rocket uAPI)
stay disabled. No npu_opp_table — devfreq is stubbed.

Kernel config: ROCKCHIP_RKNPU=y + DEBUG_FS + DRM_GEM, FENCE/SRAM off
(fence_fd stays -1, matching the RE line's driver contract).
